msgid "The following program builds the journal and checks these results with the `ExchangeAlgebra` module:"
msgstr "次のプログラムは `ExchangeAlgebra` モジュールで仕訳帳を構築し, これらの結果を確かめます:"

#: src/overview.md:57
msgid "It prints:"
msgstr "出力は次のとおりです:"

#: src/overview.md:65
msgid "`.@` attaches an amount to a hat base, and `.+` adds postings. `norm` sums the amounts, and `bar` applies bar to the cash postings selected by `projByAccountTitle`."
msgstr "`.@` は金額を hat 基底に付け, `.+` は項を加えます. `norm` は金額を合計し, `bar` は `projByAccountTitle` で選んだ現金の項に bar を適用します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:3
msgid "Bases and postings"
msgstr "基底と項"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:5
msgid "A base is a tuple of coordinates, one per axis. For example, an account and a firm form a two-axis base. A query matches a stored base when every coordinate either equals the stored coordinate or carries the wildcard (#) in the query. A stored # records an inapplicable axis. A query for a specific firm therefore skips a posting whose firm coordinate is #."
msgstr "基底は, 各軸の座標を 1 つずつ持つタプルです. 例えば, 勘定と企業は 2 軸の基底を構成します. 問い合わせのすべての座標が, 保存された基底の座標と等しいか wildcard (ワイルドカード) の # であるとき, 問い合わせはその基底に一致します. 保存された # は, その軸が該当しないことを表します. したがって, 特定の企業を指定した問い合わせでは, 企業の座標が # の項は選ばれません."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:7
msgid "Definition 1 of the preprint gives a symmetric comparison. The library's `matchesQuery` treats only a query-side # as a pattern."
msgstr "プレプリントの Definition 1 は対称な比較を定めています. ライブラリの `matchesQuery` は, 問い合わせ側の # だけをパターンとして扱います."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:9
msgid "A hat base pairs the tuple with a direction. `Not` records an increase and `Hat` a decrease. A posting pairs this hat base with a nonnegative real amount from the value domain $V$. Use `.@` to construct a posting. `HatNot` is a wildcard for queries."
msgstr "hat 基底はタプルと方向の組です. `Not` は増加を, `Hat` は減少を記録します. 項 (posting) は, この hat 基底と値域 $V$ に属する非負実数の金額の組です. 項の構築には `.@` を使ってください. `HatNot` は問い合わせ用の wildcard です."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:11
msgid "At each underlying base $e_i$, a redundant algebra element records two finite sequences of amounts. Write $f_i(e_i)=\\langle A_i,B_i\\rangle$, with $A_i$ the `Not` sequence and $B_i$ the `Hat` sequence. Two increases of 3 and 2 at the same base remain separate postings until an operation explicitly combines them."
msgstr "冗長代数の要素は, hat を除いた各基底 $e_i$ に金額の有限列を 2 つ記録します. $f_i(e_i)=\\langle A_i,B_i\\rangle$ と書き, $A_i$ を `Not` の列, $B_i$ を `Hat` の列とします. 同じ基底の 3 と 2 という 2 件の増加は, 明示的にまとめる演算を適用するまで別々の項として残ります."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:13
msgid "Operations"
msgstr "演算"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:15
msgid "The following methods belong to `Redundant` in `ExchangeAlgebra.Algebra.Core.Representation`. In their signatures, `n` is the amount type, `b` the hat base type, and `a n b` the algebra element."
msgstr "次のメソッドは `ExchangeAlgebra.Algebra.Core.Representation` の `Redundant` に属します. 型シグネチャの `n` は金額の型, `b` は hat 基底の型, `a n b` は代数の要素です."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:17
msgid "Operation"
msgstr "演算"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:17
msgid "Method and type"
msgstr "メソッドと型"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:17
msgid "Effect"
msgstr "作用"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:19
msgid "Hat"
msgstr "hat"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:19
msgid "`(.^) :: a n b -> a n b`"
msgstr "`(.^) :: a n b -> a n b`"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:19
msgid "Swap the two sequences<br>at each base, preserving<br>every amount."
msgstr "各基底の 2 つの列を<br>入れ替えます. すべての<br>金額を保持します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:20
msgid "Bar"
msgstr "bar"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:20
msgid "`(.-) :: a n b -> a n b`"
msgstr "`(.-) :: a n b -> a n b`"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:20
msgid "Total each sequence at<br>each base and cancel the<br>two totals. Keep the<br>excess on the larger side<br>and drop a zero remainder."
msgstr "各基底で各列を合計し,<br>両方の合計を相殺します.<br>大きい側に差額を残し,<br>残額がゼロなら除きます."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:21
msgid "Sum"
msgstr "和"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:21
msgid "`(.+) :: a n b -> a n b -> a n b`"
msgstr "`(.+) :: a n b -> a n b -> a n b`"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:21
msgid "Concatenate the<br>corresponding sequences."
msgstr "対応する列を<br>連結します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:22
msgid "Scalar<br>multiplication"
msgstr "スカラー倍"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:22
msgid "`(.*) :: n -> a n b -> a n b`"
msgstr "`(.*) :: n -> a n b -> a n b`"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:22
msgid "Multiply every amount by<br>the same finite<br>nonnegative scalar."
msgstr "すべての金額に同じ有限の<br>非負スカラーを掛けます."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:23
msgid "Norm"
msgstr "norm"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:23
msgid "`norm :: a n b -> n`"
msgstr "`norm :: a n b -> n`"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:23
msgid "Sum all amounts on both<br>sides over all bases."
msgstr "すべての基底の両側の<br>金額を合計します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:24
msgid "Compression"
msgstr "compress"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:24
msgid "`compress :: a n b -> a n b`"
msgstr "`compress :: a n b -> a n b`"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:24
msgid "Sum amounts with the<br>same base and direction,<br>keeping opposite<br>directions separate."
msgstr "基底と方向が同じ金額を<br>合計します. 反対方向の<br>金額は別々に保ちます."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:26
msgid "For example, two `Not` amounts of 3 and 2 and a `Hat` amount of 4 on the same base have norm 9. Compression gives 5 on `Not` and 4 on `Hat`. Bar leaves 1 on `Not`. In general, if the two sequences at a base have lengths $p_i$ and $q_i$, their contribution to the norm is"
msgstr "例えば, 同じ基底に `Not` の金額 3 と 2, `Hat` の金額 4 があるとき, norm は 9 です. compress を適用すると `Not` に 5, `Hat` に 4 が残ります. bar を適用すると `Not` に 1 が残ります. 一般に, ある基底の 2 つの列の長さが $p_i$ と $q_i$ であるとき, その基底の norm への寄与は次のとおりです:"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:28
msgid "$$ \\\\operatorname{norm}(f_i(e_i)) = \\sum\\_{j=1}^{p_i} a\\_{ij} + \\sum\\_{k=1}^{q_i} b\\_{ik}. $$"
msgstr "$$ \\\\operatorname{norm}(f_i(e_i)) = \\sum\\_{j=1}^{p_i} a\\_{ij} + \\sum\\_{k=1}^{q_i} b\\_{ik}. $$"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:32
msgid "Five axioms"
msgstr "5 つの公理"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:34
msgid "Let $x=\\langle f_1,\\ldots,f_n\\rangle$ and let $a$ be a nonnegative scalar."
msgstr "$x=\\langle f_1,\\ldots,f_n\\rangle$ とし, $a$ を非負スカラーとします."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:36
msgid "**Hat is an involution.** Applying hat twice restores the original postings."
msgstr "**hat の対合性.** hat を 2 回適用すると元の項に戻ります."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:38
msgid "$$ \\\\widehat{\\widehat{f_i}}(e_i) = f_i(e_i). $$"
msgstr "$$ \\\\widehat{\\widehat{f_i}}(e_i) = f_i(e_i). $$"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:42
msgid "**Scaling at one base.** The scalar acts on each amount in each sequence."
msgstr "**1 つの基底でのスカラー倍.** スカラーは各列の各金額に作用します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:44
msgid "$$ a \\ast f_i(e_i) = \\langle a \\ast A_i, a \\ast B_i\\rangle. $$"
msgstr "$$ a \\ast f_i(e_i) = \\langle a \\ast A_i, a \\ast B_i\\rangle. $$"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:48
msgid "**Scaling across bases.** The scalar acts on every component."
msgstr "**基底全体のスカラー倍.** スカラーはすべての成分に作用します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:50
msgid "$$ a \\ast \\langle f_1,\\ldots,f_n\\rangle = \\langle a \\ast f_1,\\ldots,a \\ast f_n\\rangle. $$"
msgstr "$$ a \\ast \\langle f_1,\\ldots,f_n\\rangle = \\langle a \\ast f_1,\\ldots,a \\ast f_n\\rangle. $$"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:54
msgid "**Norm homogeneity.** Scaling the postings scales their total."
msgstr "**norm の斉次性.** 項をスカラー倍すると, 合計も同じスカラー倍になります."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:56
msgid "$$ \\\\operatorname{norm}(a \\ast x) = a \\cdot \\operatorname{norm}(x), \\qquad a \\ge 0. $$"
msgstr "$$ \\\\operatorname{norm}(a \\ast x) = a \\cdot \\operatorname{norm}(x), \\qquad a \\ge 0. $$"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:60
msgid "**Norm additivity.** Adding postings adds their totals."
msgstr "**norm の加法性.** 項を加えると, それぞれの合計も加わります."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:62
msgid "$$ \\\\operatorname{norm}(f_i(e_i)+g_i(e_i)) = \\operatorname{norm}(f_i(e_i)) + \\operatorname{norm}(g_i(e_i)). $$"
msgstr "$$ \\\\operatorname{norm}(f_i(e_i)+g_i(e_i)) = \\operatorname{norm}(f_i(e_i)) + \\operatorname{norm}(g_i(e_i)). $$"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:66
msgid "The preprint lists the defining sum of the norm under the name “norm homogeneity.” The homogeneity law above follows from that sum and the scalar product."
msgstr "プレプリントでは, norm を定義する和を「norm の斉次性」という名称で挙げています. ここに示した斉次性の法則は, その和とスカラー倍から導かれます."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:68
msgid "For `MoneyDecimal`, axioms 4 and 5 hold exactly when the amounts and products are representable. For `MoneyDouble`, `norm` sums the stored posting amounts exactly and rounds once at the end. The two sides of a law can therefore differ in the last digit: scaling can round individual products, and adding two norms can use two already rounded totals."
msgstr "`MoneyDecimal` では, 金額と積が表現可能な場合に公理 4 と 5 が厳密に成り立ちます. `MoneyDouble` では, `norm` は保存された項の金額を厳密に合計し, 最後に 1 回だけ丸めます. そのため, 法則の両辺が最終桁で異なることがあります. スカラー倍では個々の積が丸められ, 2 つの norm の加算では丸め済みの合計を 2 つ使う場合があるためです."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:70
msgid "Account classes and sides"
msgstr "勘定の区分と貸借"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:72
msgid "An exchange base carries an account title. `ExBaseClass.whatDiv` identifies its division, and `ExBaseClass.whichSide` combines its home side with the hat direction. For ordinary accounts the assignment is:"
msgstr "交換代数の基底は勘定科目を持ちます. `ExBaseClass.whatDiv` はその区分を識別し, `ExBaseClass.whichSide` は本来の側 (借方か貸方か)と hat の方向を組み合わせます. 通常の勘定では次の対応になります:"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:74
msgid "Division"
msgstr "区分"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:74
msgid "Increase (`Not`)"
msgstr "増加 (`Not`)"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:74
msgid "Decrease (`Hat`)"
msgstr "減少 (`Hat`)"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:76
msgid "Assets, expenses (costs)"
msgstr "資産, 費用 (原価)"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:77
msgid "Liabilities, equity, revenue"
msgstr "負債, 純資産, 収益"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:79
msgid "A contra account reverses the home side of its division before the hat direction is applied."
msgstr "評価勘定では, hat の方向を適用する前に, 所属する区分の本来の側 (借方か貸方か)を反転させます."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:81
msgid "Debit and credit decomposition"
msgstr "借方と貸方への分解"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:83
msgid "`Exchange` in `ExchangeAlgebra.Accounting.Exchange` provides the two side projections. `decL :: a n b -> a n b` selects the debit postings (left), and `decR :: a n b -> a n b` selects the credit postings (right). For example, a decrease in cash appears in `decR` and an increase in an ordinary expense appears in `decL`. `balance :: a n b -> Bool` compares the exact debit and credit totals before rounding and returns `True` when they agree for finite postings."
msgstr "`ExchangeAlgebra.Accounting.Exchange` の `Exchange` は, 借方と貸方への射影を提供します. `decL :: a n b -> a n b` は借方 (左側) の項を, `decR :: a n b -> a n b` は貸方 (右側) の項を選びます. 例えば, 現金の減少は `decR` に, 通常の費用の増加は `decL` に現れます. `balance :: a n b -> Bool` は, 丸める前の厳密な借方合計と貸方合計を比較し, 有限の金額を持つ項について両者が一致すれば `True` を返します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:85
msgid "For transfers and journals, see Appendix A of [_Accounting State Space as a Foundation for Economic Agent-Based Modeling: An Input–Output Benchmark and Inventory Extension_](https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-8485050/v2)."
msgstr "振替と仕訳帳については, [_Accounting State Space as a Foundation for Economic Agent-Based Modeling: An Input–Output Benchmark and Inventory Extension_](https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-8485050/v2) の Appendix A を参照してください."

